# Python usage policy

Python is installed in this devcontainer for ad hoc, throwaway tasks only —
data wrangling, one-off scripts, parsing/inspecting files dropped into the
project, quick calculations. It is NOT part of this project's stack.

- Do not write application logic, API routes, build tooling, or anything
  that ships to production in Python. This is a Next.js/TypeScript project;
  use TS/Node for anything that becomes part of the codebase.
- Scratch scripts belong in a gitignored `/scratch` or `/tmp` folder, not
  mixed into `src/`, `app/`, or other project source directories.
- If a task seems to call for a Python script, first consider whether it's
  actually a one-off (fine) or something that should be a proper Node
  script or app feature (write it in TS instead).
- Never add `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, or any Python dependency
  file to the repo without explicit confirmation — if a Python package is
  needed for a scratch task, install it into a local venv
  (`python3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate && pip install ...`),
  not system-wide.
- Do not use `pip install --break-system-packages` — use a venv instead.
